-RVR_54=WireGuard targets need a hardware-acceleration bypass (the same one VPN Director uses). A source rule bypasses only that address; a destination or MAC rule bypasses the whole LAN, so LAN traffic loses hardware acceleration while such a rule exists. The rule is fail-closed: if the WireGuard client is down, the selected traffic is blocked, not leaked.
-RVR_54b=accel bypass: whole LAN
-RVR_55=accel bypass: this source
-RVR_56=client not enabled - traffic blocked
-RVR_57=Rules go live when you apply and are reverted automatically unless you keep them within the auto-revert timer (set on the Firewall page).
-RVR_58=IPv6 is covered: a destination list matches its IPv6 addresses and a MAC rule follows the device on both families. If the chosen tunnel carries no IPv6, the selected IPv6 traffic is blocked rather than leaked around it.
